/elasticsearch/index/mapper/MapperServiceTestCase.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":11959,"endPos":12526,"startLine":272,"startLineOffset":19,"endLine":286,"endLineOffset":13,"length":568}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":12224,"endPos":12812,"startLine":279,"startLineOffset":12,"endLine":293,"endLineOffset":14,"length":589},{"pos":12826,"endPos":13051,"startLine":295,"startLineOffset":12,"endLine":297,"endLineOffset":13,"length":226},{"pos":13072,"endPos":13085,"startLine":299,"startLineOffset":19,"endLine":299,"endLineOffset":32,"length":14}]}]},{"comment":"Two new well-named constants for the keyed-field protocol. No issues.","nodes":[{"id":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DataStreamTimestampFieldMapper.java-server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DataStreamTimestampFieldMapper.java--1512:1597","promptId":"#YWF65","srcPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DataStreamTimestampFieldMapper.java","dstPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DataStreamTimestampFieldMapper.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":1512,"endPos":1597,"startLine":38,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":38,"endLineOffset":89,"length":86}]},{"id":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DataStreamTimestampFieldMapper.java-server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DataStreamTimestampFieldMapper.java--1438:1507","promptId":"#ZXVD1","srcPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DataStreamTimestampFieldMapper.java","dstPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DataStreamTimestampFieldMapper.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":1438,"endPos":1507,"startLine":37,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":37,"endLineOffset":73,"length":70}]}]},{"comment":"The key addition: when a `@timestamp` date field is indexed and the data-stream timestamp mapper is enabled, the raw timestamp is stashed via `onlyAddKey` for O(1) retrieval downstream. The multiple-values flag is set on the second occurrence. The guard `existingField \u003d\u003d null` / flag-null check prevents the `IllegalStateException` that `onlyAddKey` would throw on duplicate keys. Logic is correct.\nOne minor observation: the `TIMESTAMP_MULTIPLE_VALUES_FLAG` is created as a `StoredField` with `new byte[0]`. Since `onlyAddKey` explicitly does *not* add the field to the Lucene document\u0027s field list (per the `LuceneDocument` contract), the `StoredField` type is never actually persisted. However, using a `StoredField` here is slightly misleading to readers who might assume it gets stored. A `LongField(key, 0L, Field.Store.NO)` or a simple marker would better signal \"this is just an in-memory flag.\" This is cosmetic, not a bug.","nodes":[{"id":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DateFieldMapper.java-server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DateFieldMapper.java--38570:38662,38671:38728,38737:38791,38800:38802,38811:38872,38881:38942,38951:40010","promptId":"#QFEZC","srcPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DateFieldMapper.java","dstPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DateFieldMapper.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":38570,"endPos":38662,"startLine":950,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":950,"endLineOffset":100,"length":93},{"pos":38671,"endPos":38728,"startLine":951,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":951,"endLineOffset":65,"length":58},{"pos":38737,"endPos":38791,"startLine":952,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":952,"endLineOffset":62,"length":55},{"pos":38800,"endPos":38802,"startLine":953,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":953,"endLineOffset":10,"length":3},{"pos":38811,"endPos":38872,"startLine":954,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":954,"endLineOffset":69,"length":62},{"pos":38881,"endPos":38942,"startLine":955,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":955,"endLineOffset":69,"length":62},{"pos":38951,"endPos":40010,"startLine":956,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":972,"endLineOffset":9,"length":1060}]}]},{"comment":"The test now uses `TestMapperServiceBuilder` with `applyDefaultMapping(false)` to avoid the newly-applied default mapping interfering with the routing-forbidden assertion. Correct and necessary given the builder change.","nodes":[{"id":"server/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/index/TimeSeriesModeTests.java-server/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/index/TimeSeriesModeTests.java-6833:6852-6743:6841,6940:6951","promptId":"#FKV4A","srcPath":"server/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/index/TimeSeriesModeTests.java","dstPath":"server/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/index/TimeSeriesModeTests.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":6833,"endPos":6852,"startLine":126,"startLineOffset":18,"endLine":126,"endLineOffset":37,"length":20}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":6743,"endPos":6841,"startLine":124,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":124,"endLineOffset":106,"length":99},{"pos":6940,"endPos":6951,"startLine":127,"startLineOffset":18,"endLine":127,"endLineOffset":29,"length":12}]}]},{"comment":"`TsidExtractingIdFieldMapper` now reads the timestamp via `getByKey(TIMESTAMP_VALUE_KEY)` instead of `getField(DEFAULT_PATH)`. Consistent with the new protocol. Correct.","nodes":[{"id":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/TsidExtractingIdFieldMapper.java-server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/TsidExtractingIdFieldMapper.java-1989:1997,1998:2041-1989:1997,1998:2048","promptId":"#S02V5","srcPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/TsidExtractingIdFieldMapper.java","dstPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/TsidExtractingIdFieldMapper.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":1989,"endPos":1997,"startLine":49,"startLineOffset":64,"endLine":49,"endLineOffset":72,"length":9},{"pos":1998,"endPos":2041,"startLine":49,"startLineOffset":73,"endLine":49,"endLineOffset":116,"length":44}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":1989,"endPos":1997,"startLine":49,"startLineOffset":64,"endLine":49,"endLineOffset":72,"length":9},{"pos":1998,"endPos":2048,"startLine":49,"startLineOffset":73,"endLine":49,"endLineOffset":123,"length":51}]}]},{"comme